    {
      "path": "src/features/aiContentGenerator/components/styles/BottomInputArea.scss",
      "content": "Inconsistent variable import style across the new/edited partials. `BottomInputArea.scss` uses `@use \"@/variables.scss\" as *;` while the sibling partials added in this same refactor (`styles/DiffPreview.scss`, `styles/MainContentArea.scss`, `styles/ContentAreaEmpty.scss`) use the relative `@use \"../../../variables\" as *;`. Both resolve to `src/_variables.scss` so behavior is identical, but the mixed alias/relative style is exactly the kind of inconsistency this dedup refactor is meant to eliminate. Pick one convention and apply it across all partials.",
      "suggestion_code": "@use \"../../../variables\" as *;",
      "existing_code": "@use \"@/variables.scss\" as *;",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/features/aiContentGenerator/components/styles/BottomInputArea.scss",
      "content": "`.quick-action-btn` (L74-106) and `.rag-toggle` (L119-165) in the same file are near-duplicates: both declare `display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 3px; color: var(--b3-theme-on-surface); background: var(--b3-theme-background); border: 1px solid var(--b3-theme-surface-lighter); cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap;` plus identical `svg` opacity handling and the same `:hover { border-color: var(--b3-theme-primary); }` behavior. Now that they are co-located in one extracted file, consider hoisting the shared chrome into a `%chip-base` placeholder / mixin and `@extend`ing it, per the refactor's consolidation goal.",
