    {
      "path": "src/features/aiContentGenerator/components/BottomInputArea.vue",
      "content": "`BottomInputArea.vue`'s `\u003cstyle scoped\u003e` imports both `../styles/index.scss` and `./styles/BottomInputArea.scss`, and `styles/index.scss` is itself pulled in by the partial chain elsewhere. Note that `index.scss` emits unscoped/shared rules (`.ai-content-panel`, `.content-display-section`, `.error-state`/`.empty-state`, `.markdown-preview`, mixins). Double-loading it into a component's scoped block re-emits those rules inside that component instead of once globally. This mirrors a pre-existing pattern, but as this refactor is explicitly consolidating the style entry points, it is worth confirming the shared `index.scss` is intended to be imported by each `\u003cstyle scoped\u003e` block rather than once at the panel root.",
      "existing_code": "@use \"../styles/index.scss\" as *;\n@use \"./styles/BottomInputArea.scss\" as *;",
      "start_line": 269,
      "end_line": 270,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/features/aiContentGenerator/components/DiffPreview.vue",
      "content": "`DiffPreview.vue` imports `../styles/index.scss` without the `as *` namespace, unlike every sibling component which uses `@use \"../styles/index.scss\" as *;`. Using it namespaced is harmless for pure CSS emission, but if this file ever needs members (mixins/variables) from `index.scss` they would be invisible without the `as *`. For consistency with the rest of the module, drop the namespace here too.",
      "suggestion_code": "@use \"../styles/DiffPreview.scss\" as *;\n@use \"../styles/index.scss\" as *;",
      "existing_code": "@use \"../styles/DiffPreview.scss\" as *;\n@use \"../styles/index.scss\";",
